<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Granma (yacht)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Granma is the yacht that carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/che-guevara">Che Guevara</a> and 80 other revolutionaries from Tuxpan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, to eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in late 1956. They landed on 2 December in difficult conditions and were scattered by government troops, and the survivors regrouped in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-maestra">Sierra Maestra</a>. The boat is displayed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a>, and the Cuban Communist Party newspaper and a province are named after it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/granma-yacht.jpg" alt="Granma (yacht)" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Expedicionarios-del-yate-granma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
